    passage: 'During a seven-month trial in 2006, Stockholm imposed a fee on motorists entering the city center on weekdays, and traffic crossing the charging boundary decreased by approximately one-fifth. Several merchants operating stores inside the boundary contended that the charge had discouraged shoppers from visiting the city center, presenting declines in their own revenue during the trial as evidence that the policy had damaged retail businesses throughout the charging zone.',
