    passage: 'The duck-billed dinosaur Parasaurolophus bore a long, hollow crest that swept back from its skull and enclosed looping nasal passages. Paleontologist David Weishampel argued in 1981 that the crest functioned as a resonating chamber, amplifying low-frequency calls that adults used to communicate across considerable distances, much as the long tubing of a brass instrument deepens and strengthens the tones it produces.',
